### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. State set + order (50 states, alphabetical in the specimen) — labels, per-state Dem/Rep shares (grey = remainder), winner side derived (larger share), per-state loserUnits.
2. Bar geometry — count, pitch, gap ratio, field position/size, baseline.
3. Stacked scale — shares map linearly to field height (100% = full height).
4. Majority line — presence, height fraction (≈0.55 of field height from baseline), colour/width, removal at flatten.
5. Annotation — arc count (2), colour (yellow), width, draw durations/order, arc paths (under-blue sweep, over-red sweep).
6. Timing — growth duration + per-bar stagger, hold, annotation start/duration, flatten start/duration + stagger, shrink start/duration, dots start/duration + stagger, final hold, total duration.
7. Palette — paper ground, Dem blue, Rep red, other grey, line ink, annotation yellow.
8. Flatten rule — segments morph so the winner's colour takes the full bar (loser+grey erased by growth of the winner segment).
9. Strip — final solid strip height fraction of field height.
10. Dotted extension — dot radius, dot pitch, dots-per-unit scale (count = round(loserUnits × scale)), dot colour rule (winner's colour, per census), growth easing.
11. Labels — state-name text, font family/size, rotation angle, fade at flatten.
12. Easing — growth/flatten/shrink easing names.

